// Grace's shop. It held the six Graceful pieces at Old School's mark prices and was emptied on
// 2026-10-04 because the owner was implementing Graceful another way - which turned out to be the
// skilling-outfit roll on agility xp. So the set is not for sale and never will be; what she sells
// is the nine recolour KITS, one per rooftop course (skilling_outfits/configs/graceful_colours.obj).
//
// allstock=no matters even with no stock: with allstock=yes an empty shop will buy ANY item, so
// a player could turn a bronze dagger into Marks of Grace.
[grace_shop]
scope=shared
// NINE, one per rooftop course - the shop was sized 6 for the six graceful pieces it used to hold.
size=9
restock=yes
stackall=no
allstock=no
// One of each kit, always in stock. restock=yes brings them back, and the price is each kit's own
// cost= (50 marks) against shop_sell_multiplier 1000 per mille on the npc - so a kit costs 50 and
// shop_delta=0 stops that drifting with how many she holds.
//
// THE RESTOCK RATE WAS 0 AND IT MEANT "NEVER", fixed 12 October. "restock=yes" is not enough on its
// own: World.processCleanup tops a slot up with `item.count < stockcount && tick % stockrate == 0`,
// and a rate of 0 makes that modulo NaN, which is never 0. Rate 1 refills on the next tick, which
// is what a fixed-price reward wants.
//
// The rate was only half of it. The other half was in the engine: a non-stackable item could not be
// restocked into its own count-0 slot at all, so even a correct rate would not have brought a kit
// back. Both were found by the vote shop's sim and both are fixed; the graceful sim bought one kit
// and passed, which is why neither was caught when this shop shipped.
stock1=graceful_kit_draynor,1,1
stock2=graceful_kit_alkharid,1,1
stock3=graceful_kit_varrock,1,1
stock4=graceful_kit_canifis,1,1
stock5=graceful_kit_falador,1,1
stock6=graceful_kit_seers,1,1
stock7=graceful_kit_pollnivneach,1,1
stock8=graceful_kit_rellekka,1,1
stock9=graceful_kit_ardougne,1,1
